  "notes": "Broward County punk-rap, and the research is blunt that the sample choice rather than the harmony carries the identity: a kitsch, nostalgic, video-game-adjacent palette over static i or i–VII. So `timbreHint` is `video_game_lead`, the chord list is two families deep, and the variety lives in `melody.densityPerBar` 5–9, which is the busiest loop in this batch — the research calls the note density moderate-high in the loop and low in the harmony, and those are two different fields. The bass is the real fingerprint: `bassline.rhythm` is `offbeat_8ths`, not the lane's `mirror_kick`, because the research says the 808 punches in on the off-16ths so it interlocks with the flow rather than sustaining — which is also why `anticipationProb` is 0.4 and `bass808.sustain` is staccato with a 20–60ms portamento for the short glides. `bass808.register` is authored to the documented A0–C2 (MIDI 21–36) rather than inherited. `hihat.fillDensity` is 0.7 for the continuous 32nd rolls under hooks and `bass808.clipping` is on for the Ronny J drum bus. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates identity and chart status medium-high but the parameters only medium and marks the tempi `[LOW-CONF]`: the 140–160 range and the drum placements are the inferred parameters — no interview establishes them. ⚠ The 32nd hat rolls are carried by `fillDensity` and by `rolls.freqPerBar` at the top of this batch's band; the roll vocabulary itself is held to 16ths at one position so this batch's fills stay distinguishable.",
